===Etymology 2===
[[File:Carquois.jpg|thumb|upright]]
{{etymid|fi|quiver}}
Possibly a backformation based on ''viineke'', an irregular dialectal variant of {{m|fi|viileke||band, strap}}, from the same root ''√viile-'' as {{m|fi|viiltää||to slit}}, from older ''*vije-''. Though appearing in writing since the 16th century, the word is unattested in colloquial speech and may be an old literary coinage.

